 ## Evaluation
 
+**Evaluation caveat:** The published results below are a historical full-corpus regression snapshot, not a held-out test. They do not measure generalization to unseen campaigns. Use a manifest with known campaign groups and evaluate `--only test` before making generalization claims.
+
 The final evaluation run contains **1,350 emails**: 690 samples from [Phishing Pot](https://github.com/rf-peixoto/phishing_pot) and 660 legitimate emails from a modern personal-mail sample (`legit/mine_modern` in the report).
 Phishing Pot is a community-collected phishing feed, and its samples can include spam or other unwanted messages that are not necessarily credential theft or malicious phishing. The results should therefore be read as performance on this labeled corpus, not as a definitive estimate of real-world phishing detection. During manual follow-up, some messages missed by Arer were also not flagged as phishing by commercial `.eml` analyzers.
 This is useful comparative context, but it does not independently establish that those messages are benign or that the tools are equivalent.
